"Journey through Genius by William Dunham: 9780140147391 | PenguinRandomHouse.com: Books (https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/books/321034/journey-through-genius-by-william-dunham/)\nciteturn516search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 35.2 years ago; Crawled: last month; Image: Journey through Genius by William Dunham Image ... Image: Journey through Genius by William Dunham ... ### Book Description Image\n\nImage: Journey through Genius by William Dunham Image\n\nBest Seller\n\nImage Look Inside\n\n# Journey through Genius\n\nImage: Journey through Genius by William Dunham\n\nPaperback $19.00\n\nPublished on Aug 01, 1991 | 320 Pages\n\n[Button: Add to Cart] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input]\n\nBuy from Other Retailers:\n\nPaperback\n\n–\n\n  * [Button: Paperback ] $19.00\n\nPublished on Aug 01, 1991 | 320 Pages\n\n### Book Description Image\n\nLike masterpieces of art, music, and literature, great mathematical theorems are creative milestones, works of genius destined to last forever. Now William Dunham gives them the attention they deserve.\nDunham places each theorem within its historical context and explores the very human and often turbulent life of the creator — from Archimedes, the absentminded theoretician whose absorption in his work often precluded eating or bathing, to Gerolamo Cardano, the sixteenth-century mathematician whose accomplishments flourished despite a bizarre array of misadventures, to the paranoid genius of modern times, Georg Cantor. He also provides step-by-step proofs for the theorems, each easily accessible to readers with no more than a knowledge of high school mathematics. A rare combination of the historical, biographical, and mathematical, Journey Through Genius is a fascinating introduction to a neglected field of human creativity.\n“It is mathematics presented as a series of works of art; a fascinating lingering over individual examples of ingenuity and insight. It is mathematics by lightning flash.” —Isaac Asimov\n\n[Button: See More ]\n\n#### Related Genres\n\nBiography & Memoir\n\n### Praise Image\n\n“An inspired piece of intellectual history.”— Los Angeles Times\n\n“It is mathematics presented as a series of works of art; a fascinating lingering over individual examples of ingenuity and insight. It is mathematics by lightning flash.”— Isaac Asimov\n\n“Dunham deftly guides the reader through the verbal and logical intricacies of major mathematical questions, conveying a splendid sense of how the greatest mathematicians from ancient to modern times presented their arguments.”—Ivars Peterson, author of The Mathematical Tourist\n\n\n### Product Details Image\n\nISBN 9780140147391\n\nPublished on Aug 01, 1991\n\nPublished by Penguin Books\n\nPages 320\n\nDimensions 5-1/16 x 7-3/4\n\nAuthor\n\nWilliam Dunham\n\nWilliam Dunham is a Phi Beta Kappa graduate of the University of Pittsburgh. After receiving his Ph.D. from the Ohio State University in 1974, he joined the mathematics faculty at Hanover College in Indiana. He has directed a summer seminar funded by the National Endowment for the Humanities on the topic of “The Great Theorems of Mathematics in Historical Context.”\n\nLearn More about William Dunham\n\nJourney through Genius\n\nBy William Dunham\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nJourney through Genius: The Great Theorems of Mathematics - William Dunham - Google Books (https://books.google.com/books/about/Journey_through_Genius.html?id=uHqMEAAAQBAJ)\nciteturn516search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 35.2 years ago; Crawled: last month; # Journey through Genius: The Great Theorems of MathematicsImage: Front Cover William Dunham Penguin Publishing Group, Aug 1, 1991 - Mathematics - 320 pages Like masterpieces of art, music, and literature, great mathematical theorems are creative milestones, works of genius destined to last forever. ... Publisher  | Penguin Publishing Group, 1991\n\n# Journey through Genius: The Great Theorems 